<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shin Sawbu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1394–1471</span> · Also known as Binnya Thau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shin Sawbu was queen regnant of the Hanthawaddy Kingdom in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1454 to 1471, the only woman to rule a Burmese kingdom in her own right. A daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/razadarit">Razadarit</a>, she had lived at the court of Ava before escaping home. Her peaceful reign was a time of prosperity, and she enlarged and gilded the Shwedagon Pagoda before handing power to Dhammazedi, a former monk she chose as successor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shin-sawbu.jpg" alt="Shin Sawbu" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HanTharWin · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Shin_Sabu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
